3.2 Procurement of Chicks
Sixty (60) healthy day-old improved Kienyeji chicks were purchased from a certified hatchery. The chicks were carefully transported to the school in ventilated chick boxes to minimize stress.
Upon arrival:
•	Chicks were counted.
•	Physical condition was assessed.
•	Weak chicks were identified.
•	Chicks were immediately provided with clean water containing glucose and vitamins.
•	Feed was introduced after the chicks had settled.
